  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="52">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 52</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.29"/><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>E chascun seniour eit soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.30"/> serjant [en<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.31"/>] sun plege, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.32"/>, si [um]e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.33"/> le rete, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.17"/> [il<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.b"/> l’]ait a dreit el hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>Ut dominus in francplegio habeat suos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.2"/>. Omnes qui seruientes habent, eorum sint francplegii; quodsi rectati fuerint, ad rectum in hundredo eos habebunt.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="52" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="274" ed="#robertson"/>E chascun seniour eit soun serjant [en] sun plege que, si [um]e le rete, que [il l'] ait a dreit el hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>52. Und jeder Herr halte seinen Dienstmann unter seiner Verbürgung, damit, wenn jemand jenen verklagt, er jenen stelle [oder jener gehe] zu Recht in der Hundertschaft.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">52. And every lord shall keep his serving-man under his surety, so that, if someone accuses that man, he may produce that man [or that man may go] to stand to law in the hundred.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="275" ed="#robertson"/>And every lord shall be personally responsible as surety for his servant so that, if an accusation is brought against him, he shall bring him for trial in the hundred court.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="519"><ref target="clause:IICn_31">II Cn 31</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_31a">II Cn 31a</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 31 | ebd. 31a</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 519, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänzt MAT. gemäss L;</hi> qu’il alt <hi rend="italic">las vielleicht F, gemäss Cnut’s</hi> andswarie</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supplied by MAT. in accordance with L; F perhaps read qu’il alt, in accordance with Cnut’s andswarie</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XLIX. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XLIX. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qi <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qi Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne [<hi rend="italic">statt</hi> ūe] <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> si nel r. <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> si il est reté <hi rend="italic">ändern Edd.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne [instead of ūe] Im; si nel r. Io; si il est reté emended by edd.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">duos <hi rend="italic">S;</hi> seruos <hi rend="italic">Palgr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">duos S; seruos Palgr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_52.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">292</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">L braucht für ‘einseitige Haftung durch den Herrn’, wie andere, <hi rend="italic">francum plegium; s. Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 3c; ebenso <hi rend="italic">friborg s. d. Wb</hi> III.—In meiner Übs. müsste <hi rend="italic">oder</hi> kursiv stehen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For ‘one-sided liability through the lord’ L, like others, uses <hi rend="italic">francum plegium; see Gl</hi> Zehnerschaft 3c; likewise <hi rend="italic">friborg, see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi> III. — In my translation <hi rend="italic">oder</hi> ought to be in italics</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
